WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:05.850
From sitcom titans to Oscar nominees and the
character actors in between, these are the

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:12.160
people behind All in the Family who have sadly
passed away since their time visiting the Bunker household.

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:16.820
Before playing Archie Bunker, Carroll O'Connor
started his acting career on the stage in

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:19.762
Dublin, Ireland, and his native New York City.

00:00:19.762 --> 00:00:25.520
After making his TV debut on Sunday Showcase,
he went on to appear on the likes of Gunsmoke,

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:28.860
Bonanza, and The Outer Limits, among others.

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:33.649
But O'Connor's most successful role was of
course Archie, whom he played on both All

00:00:33.649 --> 00:00:36.697
in the Family and the spinoff Archie Bunker's
Place.

00:00:36.697 --> 00:00:41.471
After his time as the Bunker patriarch came
to an end, O'Connor went on to star on the

00:00:41.471 --> 00:00:44.230
TV version of In the Heat of the Night.

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:50.629
He also became one of a select few to win
Primetime Emmys in both the comedy and drama categories.

00:00:50.629 --> 00:00:56.020
Offscreen, O'Connor and his wife Nancy Fields
had an adopted son named Hugh, who died by

00:00:56.020 --> 00:01:00.353
suicide in 1995 after a long struggle with
addiction.

00:01:00.353 --> 00:01:04.660
That inspired his father to do a number of
public service announcements in the 90s for

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:07.030
Partnership for a Drug Free America.

00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:11.198
"Get between your kids and drugs any way you
can."

00:01:11.198 --> 00:01:18.700
O'Connor died in 2001 at the age of 76 from
a heart attack and complications of diabetes.

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:23.890
As Edith Bunker, Jean Stapleton was kind and
understanding, though she also had to endure

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:25.929
the constant ridicule of her husband.

00:01:25.929 --> 00:01:30.159
Nevertheless, Edith was the heart of All in
the Family, and there were times when she

00:01:30.159 --> 00:01:33.117
would prove Archie wrong and help him find
his empathy.

00:01:33.117 --> 00:01:38.140
Like Carroll O'Connor, Stapleton was also
born in New York City and also started out

00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:39.291
on the stage.

00:01:39.291 --> 00:01:43.200
As the daughter of an opera singer, the performing
arts were in her blood.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:48.609
She eventually made it to Broadway as part
of famous musicals like Funny Girl and Damn Yankees.

00:01:48.609 --> 00:01:54.049
Stapleton's pre-All in the Family TV credits
includes the likes of The Patty Duke Show,

00:01:54.049 --> 00:01:56.789
My Three Sons, and Dennis the Menace.

00:01:56.789 --> 00:02:01.539
She only appeared on five episodes of the
spinoff Archie Bunker's Place, and the decision

00:02:01.539 --> 00:02:04.454
was then made to have Edith die from a stroke.

00:02:04.454 --> 00:02:06.570
"It wasn't supposed to be like this, you know."

00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:13.489
Stapleton herself died in 2013 at the age
of 90 after a long and extensive career.

00:02:13.489 --> 00:02:17.960
Sherman Hemsley played George Jefferson, who
proved to be popular enough to become the

00:02:17.960 --> 00:02:20.960
lead on his own spinoff show, The Jeffersons.

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:25.574
On All in the Family, George was Archie Bunker's
neighbor whom he often butted heads with.

00:02:25.574 --> 00:02:30.120
As The Jeffersons theme song made famous,
George and his family moved on up from their

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:34.650
former neighborhood in Queens to a deluxe
apartment in the sky in Manhattan.

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:41.040
The Jeffersons ran for a whopping 11 seasons
from 1975 through 1985.

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:47.440
Hemsley also enjoyed an extensive stage career
and appeared on other TV shows, like Dinosaurs

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:49.440
and The Fresh Prince of Bel-Air.

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:54.709
When Hemsley died in 2012 at the age of 74
from lung cancer, his will left everything

00:02:54.709 --> 00:02:58.500
to a woman named Flora, his dear friend and
business partner.

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:03.069
Hemsley wasn't buried for over a month after
his death, because a Philadelphia man named

00:03:03.069 --> 00:03:06.440
Richard Thornton claimed to be his long-lost
brother.

00:03:06.440 --> 00:03:12.020
The drawn-out legal proceedings were eventually
resolved when the court ruled in Flora's favor.

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:17.440
Isabel Sanford played George Jefferson's wife
Louise, who was lovingly known as "Weezy."

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:21.740
Whereas Archie and George were hot-headed
and frequently sparring, Edith and Louise

00:03:21.740 --> 00:03:25.000
were always trying to figure out how to calm
their husbands down.

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:29.760
Isabel is portrayed as kind and sensible like
Edith, though much sharper.

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:34.950
Sanford was born in New York City and joined
Harlem's American Negro Theater and The Star

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:37.770
Players after graduating from high school.

00:03:37.770 --> 00:03:44.349
She made her stage debut in 1946, as she appeared
in both Broadway and off-Broadway productions.

00:03:44.349 --> 00:03:50.129
In 1960, after separating from her husband,
she and her three children moved to Los Angeles,

00:03:50.129 --> 00:03:53.080
where her movie and TV career really kicked
off.

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:57.930
After appearing in the 1967 film Guess Who's
Coming to Dinner, she caught the attention

00:03:57.930 --> 00:04:01.340
of Norman Lear, who then cast her on All in
the Family.

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:03.814
"I got something to say to you, boy.

00:04:03.814 --> 00:04:06.564
Just exactly what you're trying to pull here."

00:04:06.564 --> 00:04:12.080
During her time on The Jeffersons, Sanford
earned five Golden Globe and seven Emmy nominations.

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:17.209
When she won an Emmy in 1981 for outstanding
lead actress in a comedy series, she became

00:04:17.209 --> 00:04:20.209
the first Black actress to triumph in that
category.

00:04:20.209 --> 00:04:25.270
She died in 2004 in Los Angeles at the age
of 86.

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:30.090
George and Louise Jefferson's son Lionel initially
appeared on the first episode of All in the

00:04:30.090 --> 00:04:32.330
Family's first season, "Meet the Bunkers."

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:37.340
Lionel is notable for being a positive depiction
of an opinionated Black man, which was rather

00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:39.410
revolutionary for the time.

00:04:39.410 --> 00:04:43.970
Lionel doesn't let Archie's casual racism
bother him, as he instead laughs it off as

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:46.330
a sign of his neighbor's backwards thinking.

00:04:46.330 --> 00:04:51.070
He sees Archie as more ignorant than evil,
and often patronizes him.

00:04:51.070 --> 00:04:55.100
Still, Archie considers Lionel a friend and
even something of a mentee.

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:57.290
"What are friends for, Lionel?"

00:04:57.290 --> 00:05:01.770
Lionel was played by Mike Evans on both All
in the Family and The Jeffersons.

00:05:01.770 --> 00:05:06.470
During the first few seasons of the latter,
he marries his biracial wife Jenny, and they

00:05:06.470 --> 00:05:08.450
have a daughter named Jessica.

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:13.782
Evans eventually left The Jeffersons to work
on the sitcom Good Times, which he helped create.

00:05:13.782 --> 00:05:18.470
He was replaced on The Jeffersons by Damon
Evans, who was not related to Mike despite

00:05:18.470 --> 00:05:19.949
their shared last name.

00:05:19.949 --> 00:05:24.949
Mike Evans returned for the final season of
The Jeffersons and died of throat cancer at

00:05:24.949 --> 00:05:28.403
the age of 57 in 2006.

00:05:28.403 --> 00:05:32.404
Allan Melvin played Archie's neighbor and
best friend Barney Hefner.

00:05:32.404 --> 00:05:36.630
Before he played Barney, though, he showed
up in the Season 2 episode "Archie in the

00:05:36.630 --> 00:05:39.838
Lock-Up" as a desk officer at a police precinct.

00:05:39.838 --> 00:05:44.710
Melvin's popularity rose during his time as
Barney, and he ended up becoming a series

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:49.380
regular on all four seasons of the spinoff
Archie Bunker's Place.

00:05:49.380 --> 00:05:54.908
Born in Kansas City, Missouri, Melvin had
the sort of expressive face that TV was invented for.

00:05:54.908 --> 00:06:00.460
He appeared on such classic sitcoms as Gomer
Pyle, The Dick Van Dyke Show, The Andy Griffith

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:02.539
Show, and My Favorite Martian.

00:06:02.539 --> 00:06:07.550
He also famously played Sam the Butcher, Alice's
boyfriend, on The Brady Bunch.

00:06:07.550 --> 00:06:13.050
Melvin died in 2008 from cancer at the age
of 84, and he just so happens to be buried

00:06:13.050 --> 00:06:15.000
near Carroll O'Connor.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:20.040
Betty Garrett and Vincent Gardenia played
the Bunkers' liberal Catholic neighbors Irene

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:21.400
and Frank Lorenzo.

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:26.760
Irene is Irish, while Frank is Italian, thus
highlighting the multicultural makeup of their

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:27.960
Queens neighborhood.

00:06:27.960 --> 00:06:31.070
Irene is also something of a feminist for
the day.

00:06:31.070 --> 00:06:36.288
She's handy with tools, and she often fixes
things around her own house, as well as the Bunkers'.

00:06:36.288 --> 00:06:41.099
Archie even gets her a job as a forklift operator
at the same plant where he works.

00:06:41.099 --> 00:06:43.584
"I got the job!"

00:06:43.584 --> 00:06:44.084
"Oh!"

00:06:44.084 --> 00:06:49.660
Another Missouri native, Garrett appeared
on Broadway in the 1940s and had a contract

00:06:49.660 --> 00:06:52.401
with MGM during Hollywood's studio era.

00:06:52.401 --> 00:06:58.093
Her most notable TV role other than Irene
was the landlady Edna on Laverne &amp; Shirley.

00:06:58.093 --> 00:07:02.400
Garrett won a Golden Globe for her portrayal
of Irene, though the character was phased

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:04.139
out of the show in later seasons.

00:07:04.139 --> 00:07:09.960
Garrett's TV career continued on such shows
as The Golden Girls and Murder, She Wrote.

00:07:09.960 --> 00:07:15.598
She continued acting into the early 2000s
on the likes of Grey's Anatomy and Boston Public.

00:07:15.598 --> 00:07:20.917
She died in 2011 at the age of 91 of an aortic
aneurysm.

00:07:21.319 --> 00:07:26.430
Vincent Gardenia played Frank Lorenzo as a
boisterous fellow who loves to sing and cook.

00:07:26.430 --> 00:07:30.829
He once worked as a salesman, though what
he sold is never actually mentioned.

00:07:30.829 --> 00:07:35.889
Before he was Fank, Gardenia appeared on an
earlier episode of All in the Family as the

00:07:35.889 --> 00:07:41.327
man who sells his house to the Jeffersons,
and he also played a swinger in a Season 3 episode.

00:07:41.327 --> 00:07:45.000
Gardenia was born in Naples, Italy in 1920.

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:50.660
During the course of his long and varied acting
career, he was nominated for two Academy Awards,

00:07:50.660 --> 00:07:56.080
for 1973's Bang the Drum Slowly and 1987's
Moonstruck.

00:07:56.080 --> 00:08:02.479
When Gardenia died in 1992 at the age of 72,
it led to quite the theatrical conundrum.

00:08:02.479 --> 00:08:06.580
He was in Philadelphia to perform on stage
in the comedy Breaking Legs.

00:08:06.580 --> 00:08:09.560
He originated the role off-Broadway the year
before.

00:08:09.560 --> 00:08:13.400
On the morning of the final preview show,
it was discovered that he'd died of a heart

00:08:13.400 --> 00:08:15.000
attack in his hotel room.

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:19.890
The show went on, though, with the opening
performance dedicated to his memory.

00:08:20.110 --> 00:08:26.180
George Jefferson's brother Henry was played
by Mel Stewart, an actor, director, and musician.

00:08:26.180 --> 00:08:31.301
He was introduced along with Louise and Lionel
before Sherman Hemsley joined the cast as George.

00:08:31.301 --> 00:08:36.599
Henry and George only appear in one episode
together on All in the Family, which focuses

00:08:36.599 --> 00:08:39.979
on Henry's going-away party for his move to
Chicago.

00:08:39.979 --> 00:08:43.630
The move was a way of phasing out the character,
who never appeared on The Jeffersons.

00:08:43.630 --> 00:08:48.649
"I want to thank you, Bunker, for letting
me know and letting me see that some white

00:08:48.649 --> 00:08:51.157
folks are better than other white folks."

00:08:51.157 --> 00:08:57.010
Though Henry was only a bit player on All
in the Family, Stewart enjoyed an extensive TV career.

00:08:57.010 --> 00:09:01.630
His next project after All in the Family was
Roll Out, a short-lived series about Black

00:09:01.630 --> 00:09:03.580
soldiers during World War II.

00:09:03.580 --> 00:09:08.940
He also appeared on such shows as Good Times,
The Love Boat, and The Golden Girls.

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:12.750
His last onscreen role was the 1993 movie
Made in America.

00:09:12.750 --> 00:09:18.519
He died in 2002 from Alzheimer's disease at
the age of 72.

00:09:18.519 --> 00:09:24.281
Bea Arthur played Edith's feminist cousin
Maude, who went on to have her own eponymous spinoff.

00:09:24.281 --> 00:09:29.500
Maude and Archie often butted heads, and unlike
Lionel Jefferson, who let Archie's ignorance

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:32.691
slide with a quip, Maude was famous for fighting
back.

00:09:32.691 --> 00:09:34.221
"You're fat."

00:09:34.326 --> 00:09:39.140
Maude appeared on one episode of All in the
Family Season 1, and then one more episode

00:09:39.140 --> 00:09:43.334
in Season 2, which served as a backdoor pilot
for her own show.

00:09:43.334 --> 00:09:48.140
Born in 1922 in Brooklyn, Arthur started her
career on the stage.

00:09:48.140 --> 00:09:53.530
She won a Tony in 1966 for best featured actress
in a musical for Mame.

00:09:53.530 --> 00:09:57.790
After Maude, she landed another iconic role
as Dorothy on The Golden Girls.

00:09:57.790 --> 00:10:03.060
She continued acting into the 2000s, appearing
on such shows as Malcolm in the Middle and

00:10:03.060 --> 00:10:04.820
Curb Your Enthusiasm.

00:10:04.820 --> 00:10:11.521
She even returned to Broadway for a 2002 production
called Bea Arthur on Broadway: Just Between Friends.

00:10:11.521 --> 00:10:15.691
She died in 2009 from lung cancer at the age
of 86.

00:10:16.220 --> 00:10:20.491
Bob Hastings played Archie's friend Tommy
Kelsey, the owner of the bar that the Bunker

00:10:20.491 --> 00:10:22.182
patriarch frequents.

00:10:22.182 --> 00:10:26.300
As the place where Archie can go to relax
and have a drink, it's basically his home

00:10:26.300 --> 00:10:31.180
away from home, so much so that when Tommy
puts it up for sale, Archie mortgages his

00:10:31.180 --> 00:10:32.510
own house to buy it.

00:10:32.510 --> 00:10:37.786
This catalyzes the transition from All in
the Family to the spinoff Archie Bunker's Place.

00:10:37.786 --> 00:10:41.960
The Brooklyn-born Hastings started his acting
career on the radio, where he played Archie

00:10:41.960 --> 00:10:45.660
Andrews in a 1945 show based on Archie Comics.

00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:51.320
He transitioned to TV soon after and showed
up on the likes of Hogan's Heroes, Green Acres,

00:10:51.320 --> 00:10:52.690
and McHale's Navy.

00:10:52.690 --> 00:10:59.430
From 1978 to 1986, he played Captain Ramsey
on the daytime soap opera General Hospital.

00:10:59.430 --> 00:11:04.070
In the 90s, he turned to voice acting, which
included the part of Commissioner Gordon on

00:11:04.070 --> 00:11:08.700
Batman: The Animated Series, among other roles
in the DC Animated Universe.

00:11:08.700 --> 00:11:14.442
Hastings died in 2014 from prostate cancer
at the age of 89.

00:11:14.442 --> 00:11:19.620
Though he never actually acted on All in the
Family, creator and executive producer Norman

00:11:19.620 --> 00:11:23.250
Lear was obviously indispensable to the show.

00:11:23.250 --> 00:11:28.300
You could even go a step further and say that
he was essential to an entire era of TV.

00:11:28.300 --> 00:11:33.210
In addition to All in the Family, he helped
dream up The Jeffersons and Maude, and he

00:11:33.210 --> 00:11:38.630
executive produced One Day at a Time, Sanford
and Son, Good Times, and Mary Hartman.

00:11:38.630 --> 00:11:44.000
At one point, he was responsible for three
of the four top-rated TV shows in the country.

00:11:44.000 --> 00:11:49.420
Lear caught his big break back in the 1950s
penning jokes for Dean Martin and Jerry Lewis.

00:11:49.420 --> 00:11:53.459
Younger viewers might be more familiar with
the times that he collaborated with All in

00:11:53.459 --> 00:11:57.710
the Family star Rob Reiner, who's gone on
to have a steady directing career.

00:11:57.710 --> 00:12:04.161
Lear had a hand in Reiner's classic films
This is Spinal Tap, Stand by Me, and The Princess Bride.

00:12:04.161 --> 00:12:10.163
The Oscar-nominated, multiple Emmy-winning
Lear passed away on December 5, 2023 at the

00:12:10.163 --> 00:12:12.815
age of 101.

